1. Project Overview

1.1 Introduction

The Smart Grow Bench project is an IoT-based environmental monitoring and irrigation system designed to automate plant care using sensor data. The system continuously monitors temperature, humidity, soil moisture, and ambient light levels and uses this information to control irrigation through a relay-driven water valve.

The project demonstrates embedded system design principles, sensor integration, automation logic, data logging, and Git-based firmware development.

---1.2 Objectives

The primary objectives were:

* Monitor environmental conditions in real time
* Automate irrigation based on soil moisture threshold
* Provide manual override capability
* Log sensor readings for analysis
* Implement serial command interface
* Maintain modular and documented firmware

